  "_about": "Used only when a variant has shell_shards above 1 and tests/test_lane_helpers.sh honours OPENREPOTOOLS_SHELL_SECTIONS. seconds are the mean of six CI samples (runs 42486814993, 42494094825, 42483827674). A section named in always runs in every shard, because later sections read what it sets up (the first four: lane-start, its Amendment 6 section, lane-end and Amendment 7, whose E, LOGD, WS_S and CLONE2 later sections read). groups is a list of lists of headings that must share a shard; it is EMPTY because nothing but a probe can say which sections are independent: a static read joins 19 of the 24 others into one chain through shared fake-tmux variables, most of them false edges. Fill it from the probe, then raise shell_shards.",
